criteria:
Inclusion criteria:
(1) left-hemispheric cortical or subcortical ischemic or hemorrhagic event;
(2) stroke occurred at least 6 months prior to study enrolment;
(3) German as first native language;
(4) right-handedness, as confirmed by the Oldfield Handedness Inventory;
(5) diagnosis of aphasia with at least basic auditory verbal comprehension skills, as confirmed by the Aachen Aphasia Test;
(6) diagnosis of post-stroke depression as per ICD-10 code F06.32
Exclusion criteria:
(1) other severe neurological disorders;
(2) significant uncorrected visual or hearing disability;
(3) severe nonverbal cognitive deficits, as revealed by the Corsi Block-Tapping Task;
(4) simultaneous speech-language therapy or psychotherapy during the 3-week intervention phase
